{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Bluetooth adapter feels like a natural next choice because, like my Wi-Fi and Ethernet adapters, it adds a useful connection to equipment I already have.",
    "The HDMI cable, USB flash drive, and cable ties fit my interest in practical accessories, although I would only buy them when a specific need comes up."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The memory kits, CPU cooler, and case fans assume I am upgrading a computer internally, while my history mostly shows accessories that solve individual connection or mounting needs.",
    "The cable modem and drive enclosure require particular situations I have not indicated: replacing my modem or connecting a spare internal drive."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Buying computer accessories seems to have been treated as interest in computer upgrades generally.",
    "My networking purchases seem to have been stretched into a need for other networking equipment, even though an Ethernet adapter and a replacement modem solve different problems."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My purchases are spread far apart and address specific practical needs, so a related accessory alone usually is not enough to make me buy now.",
    "The exact connection, compatibility, and quantity matter: a display cable must fit my setup, memory must match my machine, and a large pack of cable ties needs a clear use."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in practical connectivity accessories but assume broader equipment upgrade needs than my history supports."
}"}
